course: dictionary
lesson: 7802
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The words around them tell you which meaning fits. Quarter is one of these words. «Saffie gets home at quarter to four» is about time, because the words to four tell you it is a clock time.
explain: The same word can also mean a fraction. «A quarter of 20 is 5» means one of four equal parts of 20. Ask yourself: what would fit in this sentence? If you swap in one of four equal parts and it still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
explain: Quarter can also be a verb, a doing word. To quarter something is to cut it into four equal pieces. In «three-quarters of the way», three is the number of equal parts you have counted, so three-quarters means three out of four parts.
fact: A quarter is one of four equal parts of something.
fact: «Quarter past» means 15 minutes after the hour, and «quarter to» means 15 minutes before the hour.
fact: «A quarter of an hour» is 15 minutes.
fact: In the USA and Canada, a quarter is a coin worth 25 cents.
fact: «Three quarters» means three of the four equal parts. A quarter of 20 is 20 ÷ 4 = 5.
exercise: «Saffie gets home at quarter to four.» What time is that? | 3:15 | 4:15 | *3:45 | 4:45
exercise: «One fourth (a quarter) of 20 is 20 ÷ 4 = 5.» What is a quarter of 20? | 15 | 10 | 4 | *5
exercise: The owl turns «three-quarters of the way» round. What does three-quarters mean? | Three whole turns | Four whole turns | *Three of four equal parts | Half of the way
test: To quarter a cake means what? | Bake it in a tin | Eat half of it | *Cut it into four equal pieces
test: «A right turn is a quarter turn clockwise.» Facing north, how many right turns make you face west? | Two | *Three | One | Four
exam: In the USA and Canada, a quarter is a coin. How much is it worth? | *25 cents | 1 dollar | 50 cents | 10 cents
